<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Semmering Railway</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1848–1854</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Semmering Railway is a mountain railway in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> crossing the Semmering Pass between Gloggnitz and Mürzzuschlag, built between 1848 and 1854 to designs by Carl von Ghega. With its tunnels, viaducts and steep curves it was the first true mountain railway in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and part of the line from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trieste">Trieste</a>. It is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/semmering-railway.jpg" alt="Semmering Railway" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C.Stadler/Bwag · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Semmering_-_Semmeringbahn,_20-Schilling-Blick.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
